{:adr-id "2607160919"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-3511 — Small Modular Reactor generation-operator compliance actor"
 :date "2026-07-16"
 :author "Cloud Itonami Contributors"
 :status :accepted
 :context
 "ISIC Rev.5 group 351 (electric power) splits into 3511
  (non-renewable generation) / 3512 (renewable generation) / 3513
  (transmission) / 3514 (distribution) / 3515 (trade) / 3516
  (storage), per the Swiss KUBB NOGA-2025/ISIC-Rev.5 coding tool.
  Siblings cloud-itonami-isic-3510 (grid distribution) and
  cloud-itonami-isic-3512 (community renewable generation) already
  :implemented; 3511 did not yet exist. Owner-authorized extension of
  ADR-2607121000's own Top-10 value-ranking item #6 (\"3510/3512
  電力\") to cover all three. Built as a single-actor batch after
  ADR-2607152300's documented 61% defect-rate incident -- verified,
  not self-reported."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Governance/compliance software actor for an SMR generation
   OPERATOR business -- NOT reactor physics/engineering, NOT a
   control system, NEVER performs or authorizes an actual
   reactor-safety-critical action. Closed five-op allowlist, all
   :effect :propose: log-safety-inspection-record,
   draft-licensing-submission, log-fuel-custody-record,
   draft-community-benefit-report, flag-safety-concern (always
   escalates). ISIC 3511 as a class also covers coal/gas/oil
   generation; this repo's honest R0 scope is the nuclear/SMR
   operator niche only."
  :governor-rules
  "FIVE HARD checks, in priority order: (1) facility-unverified --
   target SMR-facility record must exist AND be independently
   :registered?/:verified? in the store; (2) effect-not-propose --
   any :effect other than :propose is a claim to directly actuate
   outside governance; (3) spec-basis fabrication -- a
   draft-licensing-submission with no citation to an official
   regulator source (smrops.facts, JPN/NRA · USA/NRC · GBR/ONR
   seeded) is rejected; (4) scope-exclusion -- permanent,
   un-overridable, substring-scanned (English + Japanese) over
   control-rod-operation / reactor-trip-or-scram-decision /
   criticality-safety-determination / radiological-release-or-dose-
   authorization / containment-integrity-override /
   emergency-evacuation-order / fuel-loading-or-refueling-sequencing /
   security-force-response-decision territory, deliberately QUALIFIED
   phrases so a legitimate observed-anomaly flag-safety-concern never
   self-trips the gate; (5) absolute live-actuation request -- a
   NARROWER, SEPARATE, STRONGER check that fires only on an
   imperative 'authorize/grant/execute it now' request, independently
   re-derived and re-checked a SECOND time directly inside
   smrops.operation's own :commit node (the single node that writes
   the SSoT), immediately before any write, so no upstream
   :decide/phase-gate wiring bug could ever let a live authorization
   request through. flag-safety-concern ALWAYS escalates, never a
   member of any phase's :auto set, matching smrops.governor's own
   always-escalate-ops invariant as two independent layers."
  :module-shape
  "smrops.facts (per-jurisdiction SMR-licensing regulator catalog,
   no fabrication), smrops.registry (licensing-submission-draft +
   fuel-custody-record construction, unsigned certificates,
   jurisdiction-scoped sequence numbers, mirroring energy.registry),
   smrops.store (MemStore, STRING-keyed facility directory --
   ADR-2607152100's bug class avoided from the start), smrops.advisor
   (SmrOpsAdvisor: mock + real-LLM seam via langchain.model, plus
   TWO distinct test hooks -- :out-of-scope? and
   :absolute-actuation-test?, deliberately separate), smrops.governor
   (all checks above, priority-ordered), smrops.phase (0->3 rollout),
   smrops.operation (langgraph-clj StateGraph with the redundant
   :commit-node check), smrops.sim (demo driver)."
  :registry-and-manifest
  "kotoba-lang/industry registry.edn \"3511\" entry added via a
   sha-checked Contents-API single-file PUT; test-file corroboration
   landed via branch + gh api repos/.../merges server-side merge, no
   local rebase/force-push. Superproject manifest/repos.edn
   :extra-projects gained the single new path (diff-verified);
   manifest/west.yml gained the project entry via
   `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry
   cloud-itonami-isic-3511` (server-side pin verification passed),
   confirmed canonical via --check."}
 :consequences
 ["Extends ADR-2607121000's Top-10 item #6 to cover all three of ISIC 3510/3511/3512."
  "First TWO-TIER excluded-territory design in this fleet's governor pattern: a broad,"
  " permanent scope-exclusion check plus a narrower, separately-and-redundantly-enforced"
  " absolute-actuation-request check with a second independent enforcement point at commit time."
  "This R0 governs the SMR/nuclear compliance-recordkeeping slice only -- no"
  " conventional/fossil generation, no reactor-control-system integration, no real"
  " regulator filing integration."
  "kotoba-lang/industry :implemented count 377 -> 378 (live-recomputed, fresh-clone verified)."]
